        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Two thin coats for a film sealer, one saturating pass for a penetrating one, and the second coat inside the recoat window if there is one. That is the whole specification, and following it is worth more than any upgrade in product.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The instinct to add one more coat for good measure is the instinct that causes blistering, clouding and stripping jobs three years later. If the slab needs more protection than two coats give, it needs different chemistry — not another layer of the same thing.
          </p>
